{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/223619-how-to-go-about-making-an-effective-tail-strike-for-a-lunar-in-dbt","id":223619,"title":"How to go about making an effective Tail Strike for a Lunar in DBT?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-09T14:50:53-07:00","id":223619,"title":"How to go about making an effective Tail Strike for a Lunar in DBT?","content":"Hello all, <br /> <br /> I have been playing around with an Ankylosaurus spirit shape Lunar today. However I am having issues figuring out a way to give the DBT an effective Tail Bash. So far the only options I can see for this are the following. If I missed one go ahead and tell me where to look?<br /> <br /> Prehensile Tail: Affliction Mutation<br /> -Lowered strength and dexterity?<br /> -This sounds closest to what I need but the lowered strength bugs me perhaps add in a MS Tattoo God Kicking Boot as that deals with the Strength reduction and the extra accuracy balances out the lowered dexterity? I also could use Hybrid Body Rearrangement to take talons/tusks/horns to open the club end into blades of bone making it do lethal damage if I want to. <br /> <br /> Tentacle: Blight Mutation with ridiculous range and clinching?<br /> -This really doesn't seem right for a club tail?<br /> <br /> Multiple Limbs: Abomination<br /> -Damned Expensive at 6 mutation points, and an extra arm and hand is kind of over kill on the manipulation sort of like the tentacle problem. <br /> -This is really good but seems kind of over kill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","name":"Citadel97501","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"544"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T15:03:39-07:00","id":223644,"title":"","content":"This is only a natural weapon, right? Just use kick as a base and add Talons/Tusks/Horns. Not a big deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":815,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","user":"Kazorh","date":". 08-09-2014, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T15:39:54-07:00","id":223663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/223619-how-to-go-about-making-an-effective-tail-strike-for-a-lunar-in-dbt?p=223644#post223644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is only a natural weapon, right? Just use kick as a base and add Talons/Tusks/Horns. Not a big deal.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's actually a combat tail mutation in MoEP: Lunars - scorpion's tail. It's an affliction, but can be bought up to a blight to make it piercing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T16:58:07-07:00","id":223721,"title":"","content":"Thank you, I just settled on the god kicking boot with the prehensile tail although that scorpion tail was OK, none of them felt right due to very low damage bashing damage scores. I did end up taking HBR which will let me open the tail with horrible sharp points for +2 extra damage and upgraded to lethal if necessary. I don't even carry any other artifact weapons since they aren't necessary<br /> <br /> DBT Tail Smash:<br /> -Accuracy: 15 dice<br /> -Damage: 10B or 12L<br /> -Rate: 2<br /> <br /> Spirit Shape Tail Smash: (Just kept the tail working the same way but used an agreed stat line of 12 / 3 / 12.)<br /> -Accuracy: 12<br /> -Damage: 17B or 19L<br /> -Rate: 2","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","name":"Citadel97501","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"544"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T17:01:18-07:00","id":223723,"title":"","content":"And this is why the namesake of the thagomizer is the *late* Thag Simmons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}